 "description": "Gevertz2018 - Cancer Treatment with Oncolytic Viruses and Dendritic Cell injections original model\nBioModels BIOMD0000000816 (curated). SBML file: model.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 30 time units (SED-ML: OVDC.sedml), sampling 0.029411764705882353.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): PASS, max |difference| = 1.21e-05 of species peak (worst: Uninfected_Tumor_Cell_U)\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] 6 event(s) depend only on time (and on variables only they change): unrolled into 5 firing(s) up to t = 30\n  [info] species 'Total_cells_N' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] species 'total_tumor_cells' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] Tumour_cell_U_elimination term 1/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Tumour_cell_U_elimination term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Tumor_Cell_U_infection: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Infected_Tumor_Cell_I_elimination term 1/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Infected_Tumor_Cell_I_elimination term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] time event(s) on 'Dendritic_Cells_D' encoded as time/value pairs in EV_DENDRITIC_CELLS_D.TXT (ADD)\n  [info] time event(s) on 'Oncolytic_Adenovirus_V' encoded as time/value pairs in EV_ONCOLYTIC_ADENOVI.TXT (ADD)",
